<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_DigStratumTable.xml                UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-18
  ============================================================================
  SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S2 build pass. The first real RM_LotteryTableDef instance
  — RM_LotteryTableDef/RM_CompWorkedLottery have compiled since the
  2026-09-13 spike pass with no content Def ever pointing at them.

  4 strata (index 0-3): RollPortion clamps to the last authored stratum for
  any depth past this (Math.Min(stratumDepth, strata.Count-1) in
  RM_CompWorkedLottery.cs), so deeper digs keep rolling stratum 3's table
  while still crossing beastWakeStratumThreshold (4, CompProperties_
  WorkedLottery's own default) and signalling S3's tar beast — no 5th
  stratum needed to satisfy the spec's "past a threshold, each portion rolls
  a beast-wake signal."

  Ban #1 (sump_kit_spec.md hard-ban table, enforced at def-load by
  RM_LotteryTableDef.ConfigErrors): every stratum's authored trap weight
  exceeds its era-remains weight, and no row is flagged
  isWholeBodyEraRemains. The runtime trapWeightMultiplierPerStratum (1.3,
  RUT_DigShaft's own comp props) only ever widens that margin at depth, so
  satisfying the inequality on these authored weights is sufficient.

  🔴 Row thingDefs are a DELIBERATE PLACEHOLDER, not final loot content: the
  spec's own "XML-only ledger" gives lore-specific finds (bones of
  un-bestiaried ages, sealed §GM-tier casings, barreled tar) to the items/
  roster passes, which have not shipped ThingDefs for them yet (checked:
  grepped src/ for "Casing"/"GM-tier"/era-remains-flavored defNames — none
  exist). Rows below use only real, already-shipped, thematically-neutral
  vanilla salvage ThingDefs (chunks) so this table proves the wiring — the
  ban-inequality linter firing, the WorkGiver/JobDriver reaching a real
  stratum roll, a trap row actually arming and detonating — without
  inventing the flavor content that pass owns. Re-point thingDefs to real
  Sump-specific finds when that pass ships them.
  ============================================================================
-->
